# models/saved/.gitkeep
# =====================
# This file exists solely to make Git track the models/saved/ directory.
#
# Purpose of models/saved/:
#   Prophet, K-Means, and TF-IDF+LogReg models are serialised here
#   as .pkl files after their first training run:
#
#     prophet_model.pkl       — Fitted Prophet model object
#     prophet_meta.pkl        — Training metadata (dates, metrics, last trained)
#     kmeans_model.pkl        — Fitted KMeans model object
#     kmeans_meta.pkl         — Cluster training metadata
#     classifier_category.pkl — TF-IDF + LogReg category pipeline
#     classifier_priority.pkl — TF-IDF + LogReg priority pipeline
#     classifier_meta.pkl     — Classifier training metadata
#
# .gitignore rules for this directory:
#   models/saved/*.pkl       (never commit trained model binaries)
#   !models/saved/.gitkeep   (always keep this placeholder)
#
# First-run behaviour:
#   If no .pkl files exist, each model class trains from DB or synthetic
#   data automatically on first request. The directory must exist or
#   pickle.dump() will raise FileNotFoundError.
